{
  "description": "FR-30, FR-31, SEC-26, SEC-45. `sequences`: requests at these unix times against these limits, starting with no counters → per request `{allowed, retryAfter, quota}` (retryAfter 0 when allowed; quota true when a full quota is among the reasons, so the gate answers `quota_exceeded`). A rate-limit window opens with the first request and lasts windowSeconds; a quota (`period` day or month) counts the calendar day or month in UTC of the request and resets at its end; a refused request does not count; with several limits a request passes only if each has room, and then each counts it. `clients`: REMOTE_ADDR → the key a per-IP limit counts (IPv4 as is, IPv6 by /64 as `xxxx:xxxx:xxxx:xxxx::/64`, IPv4-mapped as IPv4), or null = not an address (the gate refuses the request).",
